What is the right way to build reusable software?
Inheritance provides a built in mechanism for sharing code however there is an alternative mechanism to code reuse
object composition - to hold an object ten just call its methods to get the desired functionality.
Problem is that when we change the functionality for that object we need to know to change it to the using classes
the good thing is that we can change the object at run time which is dope as hell in opposition for super class
for example:


interface Flyer { void fly(); }

class WingsFlyer implements Flyer { public void fly() {/*flying with wings*/}}

class SupermanFlyer implements Flyer { public void fly() {/*flying with superpowers*/}}

class Bird {

    Flyer flyer;

    public Bird() {
        flyer = new WingsFlyer();
    }

    public void gainSuperpower(){
        flyer = new SupermanFlyer();
    }

}

note that flyer was changed during the run time to 2 different types!